#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Ledger onboarding screen engine.

New starts / restart (owner 2026-11-03):
  look back / recording only -> file (existing history, import, or held screenshot review)
  -> analysis: roster, accounts, deposits, refunds, transfers, unknown payments,
     reduce_big (unknown purchases), reduce_installments (remaining payments),
     reduce_debts (one loan at a time; each fact question is skippable)
  -> history (aligned month table, evidence reads, numbered one-fact asks)
  -> conclusion -> plan_choice (reduce | saving | record)
  -> reduction target, or existing savings target, or recording completion
  -> reduce_overview (money bars, budget checklist and 100k+ list once)
  -> reduce_cap -> reduce_subscriptions -> reduce_subscription_ai
  -> reduce_subscription_cuts -> reduce_habits -> reduce_goal
  -> yearly renewal reminders -> completion / apply.
  The confirmed budget appears below today's pin blocks.
Recording is always enabled. Fresh opener values: past | record.
History analysis uses every recorded completed month; current-month data stays out.
Saved older v7 flows retain their previously chosen parts and recent-window basis.
History facts: one free-text answer for one item, or
  {"items":[{"number":1,"kind":"debt|spend|unknown","said":"owner words"}]}
Numbers refer only to the issued screen; unknown is retained without re-asking.
Loan outflows remain money out and become repayments, never gap funding.
Large-purchase fact questions use 1/2 and 2/2 only when both are present;
a single present question has no counter. Never combine their rendered asks.
Reduction screens provide answer_format metadata. Translate only the owner's
words into that format; amounts are exact won and counts are monthly caps.
All choices require an issued callback or --said. Do not invent answers/skips.
No history -> recording completion; no fabricated plan.
UI-GATE is open: exact draft text and acceptance differences are recorded in
  docs/reports/2026-10-31-ledger-redesign-step3/.

debt-known LOAN_ID
    Look up a kit-recorded owner value for the pending debt card. No free values.
known QUESTION_ID
    Look up an earlier kit-recorded subscription answer. No free values.
debt-reopen LOAN_ID
    Explicitly ask one loan's debt question again, including after onboarding.

Existing v6 states resume with their original contract below:

next [--offer] -> {question, lookup?, done}; send ask as HTML and button_rows
vertically. Answer only the issued id, using choice values or free source text.
Every answer requires --said "exact owner utterance"; otherwise show the screen.
Owner callbacks go through tap CALLBACK_DATA. Never invent answers or skips.
Funding multi-select payloads have multi=true, a grouped numbered HTML list,
numbered source buttons with ✓ marks after taps, and a done button.
Relay ask literally; never build an [[OPTIONS]] menu. Answers such as "1, 3",
"1 3" and "1,3" select list positions; done saves the staged sources together.
Order: roster -> unresolved funding only -> purpose intro/items -> income.
The file screen first shows the month-flow example; choices are capture:<app>
or file:<app>. There is no defer button. Recording is already active; leaving
this step unanswered keeps a backfill todo and one weekly reminder.

lookup-set APP capture|how found --source official --url URL --steps-json JSON
lookup-set APP capture|how failed
    Session performs the returned lookup first; cache TTL is 30 days.
import FILE [--password-stdin]
    Existing file importer, passwords stay on stdin only.
capture --rows JSON --since D --until D [--card NAME]
    Stage model readings; show and apply the existing review with owner consent,
    then answer file captured. Unreviewed or empty captures cannot advance.
answer file continue
    Compatibility for an owner who explicitly wants to keep recording only.
next can return question.auto_advance=true for the purpose introduction.
    Send its ask as its own message, with no buttons, then call next immediately.
answer review_purpose yes|change|tag:0..4|done
    One instrument at a time, inferred only from its real recent transactions.
    change opens the five shared purpose buttons; toggle them, then done.
    With no supported guess, the same multi-select question opens directly.
    Each toggle returns card_update: edit_current, fallback: resend_once.
    Edit the callback's message with the returned literal card (✓ marks included).
    If editing is unavailable, re-send that question once with its marked buttons.
    No numeric item picker, custom memo, or account-inheritance explanation.
answer review_bank_ID BANK|unknown|merge:TARGET_ID
    next folds proven bank evidence into the full roster.
    An unresolved bank question describes only this account's actual rows.
    Use merge:TARGET_ID only for the issued same-account confirmation.
answer review_roster 'NUMBER CORRECTED_NAME_OR_PAYMENT_SOURCE'
answer review_roster '{"corrections":[{"number":N,"name":"..."}]}'
answer review_roster '{"merges":[{"id":SOURCE_ID,"into":TARGET_ID}]}'
    Repoint confirmed duplicate accounts through the kit transaction.
answer review_income|review_fixed ok
answer review_person_ID yes|no|skip|skip_all / answer review_pair_ID SPEND_ID|group:IDS|cash|none|type|skip|skip_all
    Person/pair questions include card.text and literal card.buttons rows.
    Keep those labels intact. Full button labels are also accepted by answer.
    A determined candidate pick applies immediately and returns a result card
    with a correction button. Person yes --said preserves the owner's words;
    the relay may resolve the next pair directly from them, including cash
    for an off-ledger cash reimbursement (pass-through, no expense link).
tap CALLBACK_DATA
    Resolve a card button against the issued question; never sends Telegram.
answer review_odd_ID monthly|quarterly|semiannual|yearly (cycle) or transit|ok
answer review_living '{"one_off":[SPEND_ID],"subscriptions":[SPEND_ID]}'
    Map the owner's named purchases to ids in question.review; ok means none.
answer review_cards capture|captured|skip
    capture holds this screen. Read the requested card-app installment list,
    confirm its details with the owner and save through installment-add or
    installment-confirm; captured advances only after those records change.
answer diagnosis fix --fix N=... | <choice>
    Existing correction and goal actions. No balance question.
fixed-correct NAME_OR_ID cycle=yearly [amount=N] [next_due=D] [name=TEXT]
    Relay say (the tool's correction outcome), then the returned pending
    question. Figures refresh; this does not answer or advance the question.
apply --spend-app APP / apply --sweep thu@20:00
    Persist an explicit weekly source or separate sweep time after completion.
say 'OWNER WORDS' --spend-app APP / say 'OWNER WORDS' --sweep thu@20:00
    Apply typed reconciliation preferences; wording is evidence only.
say 'OWNER WORDS' [RECEIPT_ID] / revisit [RECEIPT_ID]
    Issue a fresh Candidate A correction during or after onboarding.
allocation RECEIPT_ID JSON
    Preview explicit expense shares and payers; confirmation is a separate tap.
apply / restart / propose / verdict / offered / declined / state
    Existing lifecycle commands. --today D pins dates for replays.

See README.md for the full service contract. Never sends a message itself.
"""
import argparse, datetime, json, os, sys
from zoneinfo import ZoneInfo
sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
from ledgerlib import kit, onboarding, allocation, reconciliation

CMDS = ('verdict', 'offered', 'declined', 'next', 'answer', 'tap', 'import', 'restart', 'propose', 'apply', 'state',
        'lookup', 'lookup-set', 'product-note', 'capture', 'revisit', 'say', 'allocation', 'fixed-correct',
        'known', 'debt-known', 'debt-reopen', 'allocation-undo')
ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog='onboarding')
ap.add_argument('command', choices=CMDS)
ap.add_argument('args', nargs='*')
ap.add_argument('--today')
ap.add_argument('--archive', type=int)
ap.add_argument('--sweep')
ap.add_argument('--spend-app')
ap.add_argument('--auto')
ap.add_argument('--plan')
ap.add_argument('--said')
ap.add_argument('--tags', help='instrument purpose labels from the returned fixed vocabulary, comma-separated')
ap.add_argument('--fix', action='append', default=[])
ap.add_argument('--offer', action='store_true')
ap.add_argument('--password-stdin', action='store_true')
ap.add_argument('--source')
ap.add_argument('--url')
ap.add_argument('--steps-json')
ap.add_argument('--rows')
ap.add_argument('--since')
ap.add_argument('--until')
ap.add_argument('--card')
ap.add_argument('--direction')
a = ap.parse_args()
try:
    if a.command == 'verdict':
        v, reason = onboarding.verdict()
        print('VERDICT\t%s\t%s' % (v, reason))
        if v == 'OFFER':
            print('ENTRY\t' + onboarding.ENTRY)
        sys.exit(0 if v == 'OFFER' else 3)
    if a.command in ('offered', 'declined'):
        st = onboarding.record(a.command)
        print(json.dumps({'offers': st.get('offers', 0), 'declines': st.get('declines', 0)}))
        sys.exit(0)
    if a.command == 'state':
        print(json.dumps(onboarding.load_state(), ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True))
        sys.exit(0)
    today = (datetime.date.fromisoformat(a.today) if a.today else
             datetime.datetime.now(ZoneInfo('Asia/Seoul')).date())
    if a.command == 'fixed-correct':
        if len(a.args) < 2 or any('=' not in field for field in a.args[1:]):
            raise ValueError('fixed-correct needs NAME_OR_ID field=value [...]')
        out = onboarding.fixed_correct(a.args[0], dict(field.split('=', 1) for field in a.args[1:]),
                                       direction=a.direction, today=today)
    elif a.command == 'debt-known':
        if len(a.args) != 1 or a.said:
            raise ValueError('debt-known needs LOAN_ID only; values come from kit records')
        out = onboarding.debt_known(int(a.args[0]))
    elif a.command == 'debt-reopen':
        if len(a.args) != 1:
            raise ValueError('debt-reopen needs LOAN_ID')
        out = onboarding.debt_reopen(int(a.args[0]), today=today)
    elif a.command == 'allocation-undo':
        if len(a.args) != 1:
            raise ValueError('allocation-undo needs the linked RECEIPT_ID')
        out = allocation.undo(int(a.args[0]))
    elif a.command == 'revisit':
        out = allocation.open_editor(int(a.args[0]) if a.args else None)
    elif a.command == 'say':
        if not a.args:
            raise ValueError('say needs owner evidence; any wording is accepted')
        if a.spend_app is not None or a.sweep is not None:
            out = reconciliation.say(a.args[0], today=today, spend_app=a.spend_app, sweep=a.sweep)
        else:
            out = allocation.say(a.args[0], int(a.args[1]) if len(a.args)>1 else None)
    elif a.command == 'allocation':
        if len(a.args)!=2:
            raise ValueError('allocation needs receipt id and allocation JSON')
        data = json.loads(a.args[1])
        out = allocation.preview(int(a.args[0]), data['allocations'], data.get('partial',False))
    elif a.command == 'known':
        if len(a.args) != 1 or a.said:
            raise ValueError('known needs QUESTION_ID only; values come from kit records')
        out = onboarding.known(a.args[0])
    elif a.command == 'next':
        out = onboarding.next_question(today=today, offer=a.offer)
    elif a.command == 'tap':
        if len(a.args) != 1:
            raise ValueError('tap needs <callback_data>')
        out = onboarding.tap(a.args[0], today=today)
    elif a.command == 'answer':
        if len(a.args) not in (1, 2):
            raise ValueError('answer needs <id> [<value>]')
        out = onboarding.answer(a.args[0], a.args[1] if len(a.args) == 2 else '', said=a.said, today=today,
                                fixes=a.fix, tags=a.tags)
    elif a.command == 'import':
        if len(a.args) != 1:
            raise ValueError('import needs <file>')
        # the password: one stdin line, this call only (never argv / state / log)
        pw = sys.stdin.readline().rstrip('\r\n') if a.password_stdin else None
        out = onboarding.import_file(a.args[0], today=today, password=pw or None)
        pw = None
    elif a.command == 'capture':
        if not a.rows or not a.since or not a.until:
            raise ValueError('capture needs --rows JSON --since D --until D')
        out = onboarding.capture(json.loads(a.rows), datetime.date.fromisoformat(a.since),
                                 datetime.date.fromisoformat(a.until), card=a.card, today=today)
    elif a.command == 'lookup':
        out = onboarding.lookup_status(today=today)
    elif a.command == 'lookup-set':
        if len(a.args) != 3:
            raise ValueError('lookup-set needs <app> export|how <verdict>')
        out = onboarding.lookup_set(a.args[0], a.args[1], a.args[2], source=a.source, url=a.url,
                                    steps_json=a.steps_json, today=today)
    elif a.command == 'product-note':
        if len(a.args) != 1:
            raise ValueError('product-note needs <text>')
        out = onboarding.product_note(a.args[0], today=today)
    elif a.command == 'restart':
        out = onboarding.restart(today=today)
    elif a.command == 'propose':
        out = onboarding.propose(today=today)
    else:
        auto = None if a.auto is None else [x for x in a.auto.split(',') if x.strip()]
        aliases = json.load(open(a.plan))['alias_writes'] if a.plan else []
        out = onboarding.run_apply(archive=a.archive, sweep=a.sweep, auto=auto, alias_writes=aliases, today=today, spend_app=a.spend_app)
    if a.command in ('next', 'import', 'answer', 'tap', 'apply'):
        # Large roster payloads can be persisted/truncated by the model's
        # tool runner. Put the turn-wide relay contract before that payload
        # so the preview cannot hide it behind question/card duplicates.
        out = dict(relay=out.get('relay') or onboarding.VERBATIM_RELAY,
                   **{key: value for key, value in out.items() if key != 'relay'})
        # Keep preconditions visible even when a caller projects stdout to
        # ask/choices with jq. These are machine instructions, never UI.
        print('LEDGER_RELAY ' + out['relay'], file=sys.stderr)
        q = out.get('question') or {}
        contract = {key: q[key] for key in ('memory_lookup', 'instructions',
                    'capture_format', 'answer_format', 'principal_subtraction_format',
                    'interest_free_balance_format', 'missing_fields') if key in q}
        if contract:
            print('LEDGER_INPUT ' + json.dumps(contract, ensure_ascii=False), file=sys.stderr)
    print(json.dumps(out, ensure_ascii=False, default=str))
except (ValueError, kit.KitError) as e:
    print(json.dumps({'error': str(e)}, ensure_ascii=False))
    sys.exit(2)
